    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d550">

                <pb facs="1009" n="915" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg915"/>

                <head>No. 550.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pratt.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 9,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 23, of January 21 last, has been
                    received.</p>
                <p>The portion referring to the concession made by the Shah for the erection of
                    hospital under the direction of Dr. Torrence, missionary <pb facs="1010" n="916"
                        xml:id="pg916"/> physician of the American Presbyterian Board, has been
                    communicated to the press.</p>
                <p>The Government of the United States is much pleased at the evident disposition of
                    His Majesty the Shah and his ministers to deal promptly and justly, as well as
                    kindly, with all questions affecting American interests, and you are instructed
                    to lose no fitting opportunity to testify its gratification and good will.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
